<!--
  Acknowledged API-compat breaks vs. the latest published version on nuget.org.
  Picked up automatically by ZeroAlloc-Net/.github/.github/workflows/api-compat.yml
  when present at the repo root.

  Regenerate after intentional breaks: re-run apicompat against the latest published
  nupkg with the generate-suppression-file argument.

  Justifications (3.0.0):
    CP0002 IMediatorBuilder.Create. Static interface method (DIM) replaced by the
    now-public MediatorBuilder class. Call `new MediatorBuilder(services)` instead.
    Static factories on interfaces tie the contract to a specific implementation;
    promoting the concrete class lets IMediatorBuilder evolve without breaking callers.
    See https://github.com/ZeroAlloc-Net/ZeroAlloc.Mediator/pull/63 (review item I3).

  Justifications (Mediator.Authorization 2.0.0):
    CP0001 MediatorAuthorizationGeneratedHooks. Internal generator-emitted plumbing
    type that escaped as public surface is removed. Per-request policy dispatch now
    uses DI-resolved `AuthorizerFor<T>` so consumers no longer touch this seam.
    CP0002 MediatorAuthorizationGeneratedHooks.Configure. Same rationale as the
    type-removal entry above; the static `Configure` callback receiver is gone.
    CP0002 AuthorizationOptions.AutoRegisterDiscoveredPolicies. Discovery-time
    auto-registration was a generator-coupled feature; in v2 callers register
    policies explicitly via `IServiceCollection`, so the property is removed.

  Diagnostic-ID reference:
  https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/fundamentals/package-validation/diagnostic-ids
-->
